%I A002008 M4027 N1671 #27 Nov 08 2026 16:45:58
%S A002008 5,120,1840,27552,421248,6613504,106441472,1750927872,29351069696,
%T A002008 500108070912,8642742116352,151219221970944,2674731179507712,
%U A002008 47766859881578496,860375518046519296,15616190800695263232,285400996457577185280,5248597973063691141120,97071366942828779274240
%N A002008 Number of rooted planar maps with 2n trivalent vertices and a root vertex of valence 6.
%D A002008 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, The enumeration of almost cubic maps, pp. 281-295 in Proceedings of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, edited R. C. Mullin et al., 1970.
%D A002008 N. J. A. Sloane, A Handbook of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1973 (includes this sequence).
%D A002008 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A002008 Christopher Smolen, <a href="/A002008/b002008.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..200</a>
%H A002008 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, <a href="/A002005/a002005.pdf">The enumeration of almost cubic maps</a>, Proc. of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, (1970), 291-295 [scanned annotated copy].
%H A002008 Christopher Smolen, <a href="https://github.com/chrispbsmolen/almost-cubic-maps">Almost cubic maps: programs, b-files and three computations of the Mullin-Nemeth-Schellenberg table</a>
%H A002008 Jian Zhou, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.03883">Fat and Thin Emergent Geometries of Hermitian One-Matrix Models</a>, arXiv:1810.03883 [math-ph], 2018.
%F A002008 a(n) = A002005(n+2) - 6*A002005(n+1) - 3*Sum_{i=0..n} A002005(i)*A002005(n-i).
%F A002008 G.f.: (C(x) - 1 - 4*x)/x^2 - 6*(C(x) - 1)/x - 3*C(x)^2, where C(x) is the g.f. of A002005. - _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
%o A002008 (Python)
%o A002008 from math import factorial
%o A002008 def dfact(n):
%o A002008     r = 1
%o A002008     while n > 1: r *= n; n -= 2
%o A002008     return r
%o A002008 def c(n): return 2**(2*n+1)*dfact(3*n)//(factorial(n+2)*dfact(n))  # A002005
%o A002008 def d(n): return sum(c(i)*c(n-i) for i in range(n+1))
%o A002008 def a(n): return c(n+2) - 6*c(n+1) - 3*d(n)  # _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
%Y A002008 Cf. A002005, A002006, A002007, A002009, A002010.
%K A002008 nonn,changed
%O A002008 0,1
%A A002008 _N. J. A. Sloane_
%E A002008 Name clarified and a(8)-a(18) from _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
